Create two new route files in /Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Shopify App/QuizSnap/app/routes/.

First read these files to understand the codebase patterns:
- app/routes/app.quizzes.$id.tsx (to understand quiz editor pattern)
- app/services/quiz.server.ts (to understand service layer)
- prisma/schema.prisma (to understand ResultPage and WidgetConfig models)

## File 1: app/routes/app.quizzes.$id.results.tsx

This is the result pages editor for a quiz. URL: /app/quizzes/:id/results

**Schema reference:**
```prisma
model ResultPage {
  id            String   @id @default(cuid())
  quizId        String
  title         String
  description   String?
  type          String   @default("default")   // default | score-range | tag-match
  minScore      Int?
  maxScore      Int?
  matchTags     String   @default("[]")        // JSON: string[]
  productLimit  Int      @default(4)
  layout        String   @default("grid")      // grid | list | carousel
  showDiscount  Boolean  @default(false)
  discountType  String?                         // percentage | fixed
  discountValue Float?
  discountCode  String?
  ctaText       String?
  ctaUrl        String?
  styling       String   @default("{}")
  position      Int      @default(0)
}
```

**Loader:** Authenticate admin, get quizId from params, fetch quiz with result pages:
```typescript
export async function loader({ request, params }: LoaderFunctionArgs) {
  const { session } = await authenticate.admin(request);
  const { id } = params;

  const quiz = await db.quiz.findFirst({
    where: { id, shop: session.shop },
    include: {
      resultPages: { orderBy: { position: "asc" } },
    },
  });

  if (!quiz) throw json({ error: "Quiz not found" }, { status: 404 });

  return json({ quiz, resultPages: quiz.resultPages.map(r => ({
    ...r,
    matchTags: parseSafe(r.matchTags, [] as string[]),
    styling: parseSafe(r.styling, {}),
  })) });
}
```

**Action:** Handle intents: `create`, `update`, `delete`, `reorder`

For `create`:
```typescript
await db.resultPage.create({
  data: {
    quizId: id!,
    title: formData.get("title") as string || "Result Page",
    type: formData.get("type") as string || "default",
    position: await db.resultPage.count({ where: { quizId: id } }),
  }
});
```

For `update`:
```typescript
const pageId = formData.get("pageId") as string;
const updates: Record<string, unknown> = {};
// parse all fields from formData - title, description, type, minScore, maxScore, 
// matchTags (JSON array), layout, productLimit, showDiscount, discountType, 
// discountValue, discountCode, ctaText, ctaUrl
await db.resultPage.update({
  where: { id: pageId },
  data: updates,
});
```

For `delete`:
```typescript
// Verify ownership via quiz
const page = await db.resultPage.findFirst({ where: { id: pageId, quiz: { id: id, shop: session.shop } } });
if (!page) throw json({ error: "Not found" }, { status: 404 });
await db.resultPage.delete({ where: { id: pageId } });
// Reorder remaining pages
const remaining = await db.resultPage.findMany({ where: { quizId: id }, orderBy: { position: "asc" } });
await Promise.all(remaining.map((p, idx) => db.resultPage.update({ where: { id: p.id }, data: { position: idx } })));
```

**UI Requirements (full Polaris - production grade):**

The page shows a split layout:
- LEFT SIDE: List of result pages (IndexTable or card list) 
  - Each card shows: title, type badge, position
  - "Add result page" button at bottom
  - Click a row to select it for editing
- RIGHT SIDE: Edit form for selected result page

The edit form (right side) uses a Card with FormLayout:
- TextField: Title
- TextField: Description (multiline)
- Select: Type (default, score-range, tag-match)
- If type === "score-range": show minScore and maxScore TextFields side by side
- If type === "tag-match": show TextField for match tags (comma-separated)
- Select: Layout (grid, list, carousel)  
- TextField (type="number"): Product limit (1-10)
- Checkbox: Show discount
- If showDiscount: show Select (percentage/fixed), TextField (value), TextField (code)
- TextField: CTA Button text
- TextField: CTA URL

Include a delete button at the bottom with useEffect on actionData to trigger toast via `shopify.toast.show()`.

Add EmptyState when no result pages exist, with action to create first one.
Add HydrateFallback with SkeletonPage.

Use `useLoaderData<typeof loader>()`, `useActionData<typeof action>()`, `useFetcher()` for inline saves, `useAppBridge()` for toasts.

Import all Polaris components needed: Page, Layout, Card, IndexTable, FormLayout, TextField, Select, Checkbox, BlockStack, InlineStack, Button, Text, Badge, EmptyState, Divider, Box, Modal.

Import `authenticate` from `"../shopify.server"`, `db` from `"~/db.server"`.
Import `json` and all types from `"react-router"`.
Add `export const headers: HeadersFunction` at bottom using `boundary.headers`.

## File 2: app/routes/app.widget.tsx

This is the widget configuration page. URL: /app/widget

**Schema reference:**
```prisma
model WidgetConfig {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  shop         String   @unique
  position     String   @default("embedded")   // embedded | popup | slide-in | full-page
  triggerType  String   @default("button")     // button | scroll | timer | exit-intent
  triggerValue String   @default("{}")
  styling      String   @default("{}")         // { primaryColor, borderRadius, fontSize }
  branding     String   @default("{}")         // { showPoweredBy, logoUrl }
  customCss    String?
}
```

**Loader:**
```typescript
export async function loader({ request }: LoaderFunctionArgs) {
  const { session } = await authenticate.admin(request);

  let config = await db.widgetConfig.findUnique({ where: { shop: session.shop } });
  if (!config) {
    config = await db.widgetConfig.create({ data: { shop: session.shop } });
  }

  const parseSafe = <T>(s: string, fb: T): T => { try { return JSON.parse(s) as T; } catch { return fb; } };

  return json({
    config: {
      ...config,
      triggerValue: parseSafe(config.triggerValue, {} as Record<string, unknown>),
      styling: parseSafe(config.styling, { primaryColor: "#5C6AC4", borderRadius: "8", fontSize: "16" }),
      branding: parseSafe(config.branding, { showPoweredBy: true }),
    }
  });
}
```

**Action:** Handle intent `save`:
```typescript
const { session } = await authenticate.admin(request);
const formData = await request.formData();
const updates = {
  position: formData.get("position") as string,
  triggerType: formData.get("triggerType") as string,
  styling: JSON.stringify({
    primaryColor: formData.get("primaryColor"),
    borderRadius: formData.get("borderRadius"),
    fontSize: formData.get("fontSize"),
  }),
  branding: JSON.stringify({
    showPoweredBy: formData.get("showPoweredBy") === "true",
  }),
  customCss: formData.get("customCss") as string || null,
};
await db.widgetConfig.upsert({
  where: { shop: session.shop },
  create: { shop: session.shop, ...updates },
  update: updates,
});
return json({ success: true });
```

**UI Requirements:**

Full Page with a 2-column Layout:
- LEFT (2/3): Configuration form in a Card with Tabs:
  - Tab 1 "Position & Trigger":
    - Select: Position (Embedded, Popup, Slide-in, Full Page) — values: embedded/popup/slide-in/full-page
    - Select: Trigger type (Button Click, Scroll Depth, Timer, Exit Intent) — values: button/scroll/timer/exit-intent
    - If triggerType === "scroll": TextField for scroll depth percentage
    - If triggerType === "timer": TextField for delay in seconds
  - Tab 2 "Styling":
    - TextField: Primary color (with placeholder "#5C6AC4")
    - TextField: Border radius (px)
    - TextField: Font size (px)
    - TextField multiline: Custom CSS
  - Tab 3 "Branding":
    - Checkbox: Show "Powered by QuizSnap" branding (helpText: "Requires Starter plan or higher to disable")
    - TextField: Logo URL (optional)

- RIGHT (1/3): Preview card showing a simple widget preview mockup using Polaris components (not real iframe):
  - Shows a Card with "Widget Preview" heading
  - Shows position, trigger type as Text + Badge
  - Shows the primary color as a colored div
  - Static preview note: "Install the QuizSnap widget block in your theme to see a live preview"
  - Button: "Go to Theme Editor" (external link to Shopify theme editor)

Bottom of form: Save button that submits the form. Show toast on success.
Add HydrateFallback skeleton.
Use Form from react-router for submission.

Import all necessary Polaris components. Import `authenticate` from `"../shopify.server"`, `db` from `"~/db.server"`.
Add `export const headers: HeadersFunction` using `boundary.headers`.

Write both files completely. Make sure they compile with TypeScript strict mode (no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`).

